Pedal Steel Glide - a MIDI-effect plugin

Insert it BEFORE an instrument (as a MIDI insert / note FX). It turns legato
playing into velocity-controlled pitch-bend glides, like a pedal steel:
play a note within the "Legato Interval" of the one you're holding and the
held note bends into it instead of retriggering. The pitch wheel bends
everything on top; aftertouch adds a per-voice vibrato.

Each voice is its own MIDI channel with its own pitch bend, so chords glide
independently - the receiving instrument must be in MPE / MIDI Mono mode
(base channel = "Master Channel", pitch-bend range = "Bend Range").

Set "Polyphony" to 1 for a single-channel monophonic mode that works with
any synth and needs no MPE.

Installs:
  VST3        -> /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3
  AU (MIDI FX)-> /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components
  Standalone  -> /Applications

